No — this is a connection leak, not a capacity problem. `idle=0` while `waiting` climbs steadily each interval means checked-out clients are never coming back.

The bug is in `withClient` (db.js:11-16): if `fn(client)` throws, `client.release()` on line 14 never runs, so that connection is permanently lost from the pool. Raising `max` would just delay the same climb to a higher ceiling.

Fix:

```js
async function withClient(fn) {
  const client = await pool.connect();
  try {
    return await fn(client);
  } finally {
    client.release();
  }
}
```
